Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

13
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:56,780
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

14
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:14,799
Down-and-Out Poet

15
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,780
You're finally here

16
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:26,780
Wasn't there a new mission today?

17
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:27,579
Where's Lord Eye?

18
00:01:27,579 --> 00:01:33,859
Lord Yan is currently carrying out his duty as a supermarket stockkeeper, counting inventory.

19
00:01:33,859 --> 00:01:38,280
So the meeting to assign new missions is being pushed back.

20
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:41,980
As expected of the flawless Lord Eye.

21
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:43,680
Not only is he full-time and all-around,

22
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:48,000
he can take on multiple jobs and genuinely complete each one responsibly.

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,719
By the way, Dottie, can I ask you something?

24
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:53,680
What was that big book you were holding just now?

25
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:59,440
This is a historical testament to the Illumin-Eye's growth.

26
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:02,700
You want to see it?

27
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:05,640
Please, please, we absolutely must see it!

28
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:08,580
Oh, Dottie, you always love keeping us in suspense!

29
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:09,760
I want to see it too~

30
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:13,319
Alright, then.

31
00:02:13,319 --> 00:02:16,060
Today, let me tell you

32
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:19,120
all about the Illumin-Eye, as great as the sun god.

33
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:23,420
Many years ago,

34
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:25,980
Lord Eye wasn't like this.

35
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:28,860
He had just graduated from college.

36
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:30,780
Full of confidence,

37
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:33,520
he hoped to become the greatest poet of his time.

38
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:36,620
He spent his days studying poetry collections

39
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:39,080
and wrote countless poems himself.

40
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:42,259
He decided to use his beautiful verses

41
00:02:42,259 --> 00:02:44,140
to celebrate people's lives

42
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:45,700
and bring them joy.

43
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:47,820
But,

44
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:50,120
reality and dreams

45
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,080
are always far apart.

46
00:02:56,099 --> 00:02:57,940
The poems he wrote—

47
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:58,780
no one liked,

48
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:00,260
and no one understood them.

49
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:02,320
No publisher

50
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,640
was willing to work with him.

51
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:06,760
After being coldly rejected by many publishers

52
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,080
Lord Eye's life

53
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,540
fell into unprecedented hardship

54
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:30,360
The helpless Lord Eye

55
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,540
could only put his dream aside

56
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,020
and work at a supermarket

57
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:35,940
to barely scrape by

58
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:38,600
But no matter how hard life got

59
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,480
Lord Eye refused to stop writing

60
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:42,520
and kept creating his poetry

61
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:43,900
But because of this

62
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,080
he often ended up neglecting customers

63
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,639
Sorry

64
00:03:47,639 --> 00:03:52,180
Excuse me, which aisle are the massagers in?

65
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:55,360
Thanks

66
00:03:55,360 --> 00:04:05,159
I pay you to work here

67
00:04:05,159 --> 00:04:06,340
Not to have you loafing around on the job

68
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:07,060
You hear me?

69
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:08,319
You dumb idiot

70
00:04:08,319 --> 00:04:10,400
Someone like you who only eats and shits

71
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,039
and can't do a damn thing

72
00:04:11,039 --> 00:04:12,159
has no point being alive

73
00:04:12,159 --> 00:04:13,819
You might as well drop dead already

74
00:04:14,819 --> 00:04:16,819
Your crappy poems

75
00:04:19,819 --> 00:04:21,819
aren't even worth toilet paper

76
00:04:23,819 --> 00:04:25,819
Even a finger's better.

77
00:04:25,819 --> 00:04:43,699
Sweet potato, potato.

78
00:04:43,699 --> 00:04:46,879
Same kind, stored apart.

79
00:04:46,879 --> 00:04:51,500
I will, again and again,

80
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:52,800
be dead drunk,

81
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,360
to understand

82
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:57,639
that life is my endlessness.

83
00:04:57,639 --> 00:04:59,160
Pay up, you scoundrel!

84
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,920
Trying to freeload?

85
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:16,080
This good-for-nothing came to drink without money.

86
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:17,220
You're asking for death!

87
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:19,720
Money doesn't matter.

88
00:06:14,699 --> 00:06:16,760
Where is this place?

89
00:06:42,699 --> 00:06:43,440
This is...

90
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:46,660
This is...

91
00:06:54,699 --> 00:06:55,360
This is...

92
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:59,760
This is something I can't understand at all.

93
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:03,540
This book seems to be all in ancient Chinese.

94
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:06,620
What on earth does it mean?

95
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:10,780
Gah, what am I even doing?

96
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:13,200
I should find a way out of here first.

97
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:16,220
A seasoned fisherman can always weather a storm.

98
00:07:25,699 --> 00:07:27,720
It worked! It worked!

99
00:08:13,699 --> 00:08:14,320
Could this be—

100
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:16,400
As I thought.

101
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,360
As I keep turning the pages of this ancient book

102
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,340
I can see incredible visions

103
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:25,639
This is the Illumin-Eye Empire

104
00:08:25,639 --> 00:08:27,480
The Illumin-Eye

105
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:32,419
Legend says the people of the ancient Illumin-Eye kingdom

106
00:08:32,419 --> 00:08:34,360
Once opened the Gate of Ancient Civilization

107
00:08:34,899 --> 00:08:38,200
From then on, the whole nation was filled with joy and happiness

108
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:41,259
People honored teachers and the Way, and lived with civility and love

109
00:08:41,259 --> 00:08:44,700
And they deeply revered poets who celebrated life

110
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,860
Yet many years later

111
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:49,039
The prosperous ancient Illumin-Eye kingdom

112
00:08:49,039 --> 00:08:51,180
Was invaded by another island nation

113
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:52,940
In this war

114
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:56,240
The Illumin-Eye kingdom was defeated and destroyed

115
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,399
From then on

116
00:08:57,399 --> 00:09:00,340
The Gate of Ancient Civilization was tightly shut

117
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:02,779
And was never opened again

118
00:09:02,779 --> 00:09:05,259
I see

119
00:09:05,259 --> 00:09:08,899
Now I understand it all

120
00:09:08,899 --> 00:09:10,399
This is it

121
00:09:10,399 --> 00:09:13,420
This is what I've been searching for

122
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:16,039
This is my great destiny

123
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:18,860
Wow!!

124
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:19,860
Ending theme

125
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:52,560
Saying goodbye to a classic always leaves you with a sense of loss

126
00:09:52,560 --> 00:10:00,320
See tomorrow waving to me upon your horizon

127
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:08,039
Each day through sunrise and sunset, time spins into even more dreams

128
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:13,100
Awaiting every second, every moment of life

129
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:19,800
Bright eyes are shimmering

130
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:23,180
A smile that greets the sun

131
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:30,800
Bravely speak that little touch of wonder treasured in your heart

132
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:35,220
A gentle morning breeze blows in

133
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:38,519
Carrying away the wishes of all these years

134
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:44,519
It will quietly wait at the crossroads ahead, oh

135
00:10:44,519 --> 00:10:52,579
It will quietly wait at the crossroads ahead, oh